<!-- Added by Plutext Pty Ltd for the docx4j FO renderer (docx4j-fo-renderer), a modified distribution derived
     from Apache FOP 2.11: hook float-offset, fox:float-offset on fo:float (fop/CR-023); the move to the next page with the
     anchor for a float with no offset (fop/CR-033). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      fox:float-offset on fo:float: the float begins that far below the top of its anchor block, space-before
      included, and the lines above it keep the full width. First sequence: a 40pt float with a 32pt offset in a
      one-line heading with 10pt space-after; the heading is full width, the float's area is drawn 32pt down
      (top-offset), the three lines from 26 to 74pt are beside it (its foot is at 72pt) and the fourth is full
      width. Second: offset 0, the heading beside the float as before. Third: the anchor has 24pt space-before
      after a one-line paragraph; the float's top is at 16 + 32 = 48pt, inside the heading's line at 40-56pt,
      which is therefore beside the float, and the lines up to the foot at 88pt too. Fourth: a 60pt float 200pt
      down, with eight short paragraphs: the first seven are full width above it, the eighth beside it. Fifth: the
      paragraph before the anchor has 12pt space-after and the anchor no space-before; the offset counts from the
      anchor's own space-before only, so the float's top is at 16 + 12 + 32 = 60pt, not 48 (the docx4j session's
      probes against Word, 2026-10-08). Sixth: two floats on one anchor, offsets 32 and 120pt, 40pt tall each: each is
      drawn at its own offset and the lines from the first's top to the second's foot (26 to 160pt) are beside them, as
      one float; before, the second's restart from inside a table threw NoSuchElementException on a corpus document.
      Seventh: after 38 lines, an anchor whose 60pt offset float 60pt tall would end past the page's foot (608 + 120 >
      698): the page breaks before the anchor, and anchor and float start the next page together, the float 60pt down
      with the anchor's lines full width above it. Eighth: the same anchor with a float that fits (20pt offset, 40pt
      tall, foot at 668): the page does not break, the float at 628pt. Eleventh (the twelfth page): the third case's
      anchor with a top border and padding; the float's top is the same 48pt (fop/CR-023 §10). Twelfth (the thirteenth
      page): the anchor unbordered inside a bordered block; the offset counts from the anchor's top, below that border.
    </p>
  </info>
